{title: Christ Is Made the Sure Foundation}
{artist: Latin hymn, tr. John M. Neale / Henry T. Smart}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Anthem}
{flow: Opening}
{key: A}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 108}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Hymnbook (Richmond, Virginia: Presbyterian Church in the United States, 1955), # 433)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Christ is made the sure foundation,
[D]Christ the [A]head and [E7]corner[A]stone;
[A]Chosen of the Lord, and [C#]precious,
[F#m]Bin[C#]ding [F#m]all the [B7]Church in [E]one,
[E]Holy Zion’s [A]help for[D]ever,
[Bm]And her con[F#m]fi[E7]dence a[A]lone.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[A]To this temple, where we call Thee,
[D]Come, O [A]Lord of [E7]Hosts, to[A]day;
[A]With Thy wonted loving[C#]kindness
[F#m]Hear [C#]Thy [F#m]servants [B7]as they [E]pray.
[E]And Thy fullest [A]bene[D]diction
[Bm]Shed within [F#m]its [E7]walls al[A]way.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[A]Here vouchsafe to all Thy servants
[D]What they [A]ask of [E7]Thee to [A]gain;
[A]What they gain from Thee for[C#]ever
[F#m]With [C#]the [F#m]blessèd [B7]to re[E]tain,
[E]And hereafter [A]in Thy [D]glory
[Bm]Evermore [F#m]with [E7]Thee to [A]reign.
{end_of_verse}
